  "tests": {
    "visible": [
      {
        "label": "Returns index 1 when y is first unique char",
        "args": [
          "pydatapath"
        ],
        "expected": 1
      },
      {
        "label": "All repeating characters return -1",
        "args": [
          "aabbcc"
        ],
        "expected": -1
      }
    ],
    "hidden": [
      {
        "label": "Empty string returns -1",
        "args": [
          ""
        ],
        "expected": -1
      },
      {
        "label": "Single character at index 0",
        "args": [
          "z"
        ],
        "expected": 0
      },
      {
        "label": "Unique character at end",
        "args": [
          "aabbccd"
        ],
        "expected": 6
      },
      {
        "label": "Case sensitivity kept separate",
        "args": [
          "AaB"
        ],
        "expected": 0
      },
      {
        "label": "Long 70k character stream performance check",
        "argsExpr": "('ab' * 35000 + 'Z',)",
        "expected": 70000,
        "timeLimitMs": 350,
        "isPerformance": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Calling text.count(ch) inside a loop takes O(n^2) time on long strings.",
    "Instead, build a frequency map in pass 1 (Counter(text)), then walk enumerate(text) in pass 2 returning the first i where counts[ch] == 1.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  counts = Counter(text)\n  for i, ch in enumerate(text):\n      if counts[ch] == 1: return i\n  return -1"
  ],
